 ## Background
-The method is part of the TetraSDF framework, which uses tetrahedral decomposition for efficient neural implicit surface representation [S1, unofficial]. The Eikonal term is crucial for enforcing the Eikonal equation, which ensures that the gradient magnitude of the signed distance function is unity [S1, unofficial].
+Originated in the Naver AI TetraSDF project, which implements a tetrahedral hash grid for SDF representation [S1, unofficial]. The method supports two backpropagation strategies for the Eikonal term: double backpropagation and second-order dOmega, allowing flexibility in gradient computation for training [S1, unofficial].
 
